new legal action is being taken after a  deadly fire in downtown las vegas the  alpine motel went up in flames nearly  two years ago and six people lost their  lives there are now two new lawsuits in  this case one filed by a victim of the  fire a second by the building's owner  joe moller tells us how he claims he  isn't the only person responsible  i used to walk that way  a lot after the fire i just did not  natasha nguyen lives around the corner  from the alpine motel it's sad it's sad  over there it was christmas time  a lot of people lost their lives for  nothing six people died in the fire that  happened days before christmas in 2019  investigators say it was caused by a  stove being used for heat wind says it  could have been prevented people were  just  trying to get out and couldn't it's like  it was terrifying i know it was now yet  another victim is taking legal action a  new lawsuit was filed by kenneth gordon  who suffered an injury from jumping out  of a window it says exit doors had been  bolted shut forcing people to jump too  many violations too many cold violations  it was just terrible and he had him  people living like that he should get  whatever comes to him the owner adolfo  orozco is facing 25 different charges  including involuntary manslaughter and  negligence but now he is pointing  fingers at others a new lawsuit found by  orozco blames the on-site manager a  tenant the city of las vegas and three  companies connected to the building's  fire alarm system he says they weren't  doing their jobs keeping the motel safe  as more legal action is being taken gwen  just hopes justice is served for those  who lost their lives i just  say rest in peace said to the people  that god lost their lives there like  every time i go back by that  and that was joe mohler reporting  orozco's criminal case is on hold while  an appeal is being heard by the nevada  supreme court
 

